<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Chedi</h1><p class="st-meta">700 BCE – 350 BCE (approx.) · capital Suktimati</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An ancient kingdom of Bundelkhand, known from the Rigveda and the Mahabharata, whose royal name was later claimed by kings of Kalinga.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Chedis are already mentioned in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rigveda">Rigveda</a>, where a king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashu-chaidya">Kashu Chaidya</a> is praised for generous gifts to priests. Their country lay south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamuna">Yamuna</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelkhand">Bundelkhand</a>, with its capital at Suktimati, probably near modern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-banda">Banda</a>. By the 6th century BCE they were counted among the sixteen mahajanapadas.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is known of Chedi government or society from contemporary sources. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahabharata">Mahabharata</a> its king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shishupala">Shishupala</a> is killed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishna">Krishna</a> at the royal sacrifice of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yudhishthira">Yudhishthira</a>. The kingdom lay on routes leading from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges plain</a> towards the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narmada-river">Narmada</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Chedi was absorbed by <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-magadha">Magadha</a>, probably by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/nanda-empire">Nandas</a> in the 4th century BCE. Branches of the Chedi line were claimed by later dynasties, notably the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mahameghavahana-dynasty">Mahameghavahana dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-kalinga">Kalinga</a>, and medieval Kalachuris called their realm Chedi.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/chedi.jpg" alt="Chedi" width="320" height="375"><figcaption>Image: Author: JIJITH NR · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:EpicIndia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>700 BCE – 350 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Suktimati</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Kashu Chaidya</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Vedic religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Prakrit</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Chedi Kingdom, Cedi Mahajanapada</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-525&amp;focus=chedi" aria-label="Chedi on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6791 1357 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Chedi lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7253 1492h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7111 1613h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M7111 1613h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day India. <a href="/atlas?year=-525&amp;focus=chedi">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

